1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:04,100
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,221
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,740
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,917
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,420
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:15,677
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:16,820
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,197
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:34,897
We came to this new world
believing that surely someday.

11
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:37,957
We just might find the way.

12
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,357
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,217
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,397
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,400
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,017
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,777
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,200
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,840
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,857
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,837
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,657
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,177
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,877
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,680
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:14,257
Only look up, keep your
head up, way up high.

49
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:17,957
Always step up, if brains
are rough, jump to the sky.

50
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,677
Never give up, our wishes,
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,140
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:32,050
Momonosuke?

54
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:34,120
Indeed, that is my name

55
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:39,777
I swear I've heard that somewhere
before That's really gonna

56
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:43,820
bug me I can assure you we've
never met before But that aside,

57
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:45,160
stop staring

58
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,800
And don't drool

59
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:54,520
You will never make a
snack out of me If you try,

60
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:57,740
I will swallow you whole Please step away

61
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:08,197
are you stuck on this thing somewhere
you're talking with your farts right

62
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:12,977
hey hello what have you lost your mind

63
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:15,980
you're not a dragon you're a talking eel

64
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:20,500
wipe away that drool i am not an eel

65
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:27,580
looks like we're both hungry huh

66
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:33,057
don't be absurd I am a
proud samurai warrior

67
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:36,837
ten days of fasting is nothing to me tell

68
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:40,417
me who are you and why are you here oh me

69
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:43,620
Lucy I'm gonna be king
of the pirates someday

70
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:54,520
that's a joke pirates are all white of
girth quite tall in stature hairy and Crude,

71
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:57,957
their king, would surely smell
much worse than you as well.

72
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,628
Anyway, can you get me out?

73
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:00,980
Come on, eel.

74
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,257
This is your home, isn't it?

75
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:03,634
Her name's Momonosuke!

76
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:06,490
I see.

77
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,918
So you must not be from here either.

78
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:10,920
I am an outsider as well.

79
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:15,005
I only know that sick children
have been gathered in this place.

80
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,706
I know not what manner of island this is,
nor what strange fate has befallen me.

81
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,957
My misfortune began when I was discovered

82
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:27,628
as a stowaway on a
sea-faring vessel nearby.

83
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:32,860
At first, I tried to distance
myself from the other children here.

84
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:36,688
But they were so kind, and they
were quite insistent as well.

85
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,692
They're giving out food.

86
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:41,999
Aren't you hungry?

87
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,090
Heed this!

88
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:45,457
I am a samurai!

89
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:47,680
I do not accept alms or pity!

90
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:51,992
I was terribly stressed.

91
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:54,200
I do regret my brusqueness.

92
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,360
Don't be shy.

93
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:56,700
We've got plenty.

94
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:59,295
I told you I don't want any, didn't I?

95
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:01,905
But you have to eat something.

96
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,797
We're all separated from our parents,
so we have to stick together.

97
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:06,351
My turmoil is mine alone!

98
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:08,240
You do not know how I feel!

99
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,580
Hello, children.

100
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,240
I am Master Caesar.

101
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:16,180
This room is all yours,
and as long as you're here,

102
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:18,578
we'll take very special care of you.

103
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,840
Hey, you okay?

104
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:22,417
What's your name, kid?

105
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,500
I have none for the likes of you.

106
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:27,600
You hungry?

107
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:30,560
Here, have a snack.

108
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:35,200
I don't want it. Candy? Go away!

109
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:39,657
So you're telling me one
of the children ran away?

110
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:40,975
Yeah, but it's weird.

111
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,337
Everyone on the boarding
list is accounted for.

112
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:44,250
That is weird.

113
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:45,362
Doesn't matter.

114
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:47,853
Let's just split up and find them quick.

115
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:16,150
Hey, you!

116
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,550
Momonosuke?

117
00:06:22,633 --> 00:06:23,868
That's an interesting name.

118
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:26,180
This is a secret room.

119
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:27,700
It's bad to come here.

120
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:30,737
You need not involve
yourself with me any further.

121
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:31,860
Please go away.

122
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:35,097
You cannot be my friend
because... because I...

123
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:37,260
I am going to escape this place.

124
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:40,520
It's sad, but we all know how you feel.

125
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,447
Because we are the same way.

126
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:46,179
Everyone wants to see their family.

127
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:48,360
We all want to go home soon.

128
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:53,677
Even though we all came from
different islands, we're friends now.

129
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:56,320
And hey, we'll all get better, I'm sure.

130
00:06:57,180 --> 00:07:01,651
In the meantime, even if we miss our
parents, it's not so bad if you ask me.

131
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,680
The biscuit room is so fun.

132
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:05,937
And we still have each
other to count on, right?

133
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:07,961
Come back, have something to eat.

134
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:12,437
Do that, and I'm sure you're going to
feel much better in no time, Momonosuke.

135
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,837
But I, uh...

136
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:16,100
This door isn't supposed to be open.

137
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:26,560
Somebody in here?

138
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,200
That's weird.

139
00:07:44,780 --> 00:07:47,340
What did we walk into? No clue.

140
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:49,940
What happened to Momonosuke?

141
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:53,457
I think they were storing some
weird Devil Fruit in here.

142
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:54,370
Dr.

143
00:07:54,453 --> 00:07:55,919
Vegabum tried creating one himself.

144
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:58,401
I heard it was a failure, though.

145
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:00,780
Me too, but he made something here.

146
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:12,900
So, I was a human, once at least.

147
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:16,680
I see.

148
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,471
So you ate a Devil Fruit?

149
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:19,560
Well, no biggie.

150
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:22,997
Why don't you just use your
power to turn back to normal?

151
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:23,910
What?

152
00:08:23,993 --> 00:08:25,380
It's really that simple?

153
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,517
So I can do that?

154
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,640
Teach me how!

155
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:30,540
Sorry. I can't.

156
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:32,257
I don't have Snow powers, you know?

157
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:34,837
Man, I can't even see
the hole I fell through.

158
00:08:34,920 --> 00:08:37,332
How high does that ceiling go up, anyway?

159
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,673
I am eager to escape this place as well.

160
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:43,349
The children must be
informed of the truth.

161
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:45,508
I heard something dreadful.

162
00:08:45,780 --> 00:08:48,740
Caesar, he unwittingly
revealed a dark secret.

163
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:01,320
Yes, the children are quite obedient.

164
00:09:04,660 --> 00:09:07,840
They're enlarging with no
particular side effects.

165
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:09,480
But of course,

166
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:12,197
I don't expect that to last
long since the purpose of

167
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:15,398
this experiment is to test
the limits of dosage size.

168
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:21,233
Well, at any rate, I'm sure they'll
all die off in about five years or so.

169
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:27,326
Hopefully no one will catch on
and we can bring in a new batch.

170
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:34,457
That man's kindness is
nothing but a facade.

171
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:39,157
He will drive those children to an early
grave without even an ounce of regret,

172
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,540
and they know nothing.

173
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,000
In truth,

174
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:44,977
I was already on my way to warn
them of their present danger,

175
00:09:45,060 --> 00:09:48,942
but when I hid in a trash can, I
fell down to this wretched place.

176
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:51,990
Caesar!

177
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:55,780
All right, Momo.

178
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:58,398
We're wasting too much time in here.

179
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:00,540
I'm getting us out. How?

180
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:03,800
You remarked yourself on
the height of the ceiling.

181
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:05,597
I'm gonna climb.

182
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,200
Hold on to my back.

183
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:11,660
And don't worry about the
kids. They'll be fine.

184
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:14,712
My friends are on their way to help them.

185
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:16,200
Is that true?

186
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:19,080
Yeah, and they always keep their word.

187
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:21,640
Just worry about yourself for now.

188
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:25,797
I see.

189
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,560
I was right after all.

190
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:30,740
You are no lonely pirate, but a valiant.

191
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:38,020
Momo, do you need food?

192
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:39,820
Come on, buddy, get up.

193
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,981
You gotta pull it together, okay?

194
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:43,300
Pull it together.

195
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:45,460
Pull it together.

196
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:54,340
Oh, cool.

197
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:55,980
So you can fly.

198
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:07,857
I hope Nami's team's
doing okay without me.

199
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:12,680
I mean, they got Zoro, but
he's no Usopp. Hey, Brook!

200
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:15,607
Look around for some
C-PRISM stone handcuffs!

201
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:17,257
Robin's ever gonna need them!

202
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:18,340
Just count on me!

203
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:21,057
One Samurai-san and a
few pair of handcuffs.

204
00:11:21,140 --> 00:11:23,897
I would imagine both of them
must be somewhere close by.

205
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:26,333
Let's just slip through this wall first.

206
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:34,610
Shit!

207
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,320
Everybody, this way!

208
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:55,000
Just a little bit more!

209
00:11:55,260 --> 00:11:57,378
Head straight into the biscuit room!

210
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:00,252
That's all it's getting!

211
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,360
Stop complaining!

212
00:12:02,620 --> 00:12:04,120
We're trying our best!

213
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:05,980
Well, try harder, okay?

214
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:08,476
Get your ass to the biscuit room now!

215
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:10,360
We've got some kids to save!

216
00:12:13,660 --> 00:12:14,600
It's cold!

217
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:16,477
This whole room is a blizzard!

218
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:20,057
As soon as I take my coat off,
that burp woman makes it slow!

219
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:21,420
I am gonna choke her!

220
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:22,810
Stop!

221
00:12:22,893 --> 00:12:25,280
You guys can't eat that
candy no matter what!

222
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:27,200
Run away, Mocha! Go!

223
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:29,057
Just give us the candy!

224
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:31,240
You can't run forever, you know!

225
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:32,320
You're crazy!

226
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:34,237
All of this just for candy?

227
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:36,017
You just want it for yourself!

228
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:37,080
Don't be greedy!

229
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:40,206
Perhaps I can slow them down.

230
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:43,960
I'd rather you not.

231
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:45,710
Open!

232
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:59,900
You three, do something
to stop those kids.

233
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,711
You're a Logia type, huh?

234
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:03,440
All right, then.

235
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:04,740
Bring it on.

236
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:09,580
Calvin. Are you OK?

237
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:10,980
I'll be fine.

238
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,534
It was only a scratch.

239
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,877
But we had better hurry
and stop the children.

240
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,790
You're right.

241
00:13:15,873 --> 00:13:17,120
Oh no, they're leaving!

242
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:19,177
We can't let the kids get away!

243
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:20,300
Wait, Mocha!

244
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:23,837
I promised Mocha I would hold them
off so she could get a head start,

245
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:25,567
but this has all gone wrong!

246
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:27,300
I put her in danger!

247
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,320
Look at that candy!

248
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:33,097
I'm sorry, guys!

249
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:35,886
Now the choppers tell
me what this stuff does!

250
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:38,040
I can't let you have it!

251
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:41,077
Why can't you see that
this candy's hurting you?

252
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:43,160
Just look what it's making you do!

253
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:50,580
Mock, we just don't have any choice.

254
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:53,400
They said we were both really sick.

255
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:57,380
Mommy! Daddy!

256
00:13:59,260 --> 00:14:01,731
I'm sorry, but you can't see them anymore.

257
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,817
I still wish I could have said goodbye,

258
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:07,135
but I don't want anything
bad to happen to our parents.

259
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,320
But it's okay.

260
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:13,076
They said we'd be better in
a year, so let's be brave.

261
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:15,980
You have no reason to fear.

262
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:20,105
Whatever it takes, I promise I'll
have all of you sweet children

263
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:25,337
feeling better in no time.

264
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:30,000
The truth is, I lost my only
son to this deadly disease.

265
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:32,557
It broke my heart.

266
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:37,717
I'll do everything in my power to ensure
no child ever suffers from It again,

267
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:43,697
and I can't bear to see another
parent bury their precious child.

268
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:45,000
The way I had to.

269
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:50,217
Oh, I'm sorry, please excuse me.

270
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:52,617
I, I shouldn't cry in front of you?

271
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:55,137
Are you okay, poor master!

272
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:58,317
Thank you, dear, so kind of you to ask.

273
00:14:58,400 --> 00:15:02,077
Well, anyway, I suppose I should
introduce you to everyone.

274
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:06,797
These children come from different islands,
but they all share the same ailment.

275
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:07,710
I'm Uzu.

276
00:15:07,793 --> 00:15:08,800
Nice to meet you.

277
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:10,610
Candy!

278
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:14,260
Hi, I'm Dolan.

279
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:15,920
Come back!

280
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:17,510
Oh, God!

281
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:20,280
My name's Gonbe.

282
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:22,380
We need more candy!

283
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:29,416
We've got some new friends
joining us today, children.

284
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,220
All right, kids.

285
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:32,980
Be sure to play nice.

286
00:15:33,180 --> 00:15:35,277
Oh, and let me know if
you need any help, okay?

287
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,190
Okay!

288
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:37,481
Thanks for days!

289
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:42,460
Lone seemed so nice, but she tricked us!

290
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:46,140
Everything she told us was a lie!

291
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,660
You handled your treatment so well.

292
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:50,520
Have this.

293
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:52,975
It's a piece of candy from the Master.

294
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,004
Guys, we gotta get out of here!

295
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:56,120
Hurry up!

296
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:58,340
Come on, step out of it!

297
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:05,177
We have to catch up with
the children, and quick!

298
00:16:05,260 --> 00:16:06,090
Let's go!

299
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:09,340
Hey! Huh?

300
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,574
You really think you can just run away?

301
00:16:12,860 --> 00:16:14,331
Saru, what are you doing?

302
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:16,846
Don't you dare try to get me!

303
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:18,613
What is wrong with you?

304
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,840
You can't just use me as a shield!

305
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,160
That's too bad.

306
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:28,377
Why are you attacking them?

307
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:29,931
They're no threat to you.

308
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,980
Get out of the way, Zoro.

309
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:39,980
Heat egg!

310
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,620
I figured melting her would work.

311
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:48,317
There's more where that
came from, BirdBrain!

312
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:50,720
So she's the one worth 16 million.

313
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,944
Hey, enough hiding in the snow!

314
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:59,336
You want to finish this or
not, you oversized chicken?

315
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:01,900
Look at the door! What's happening?

316
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:04,960
Snow fence.

317
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:07,130
No!

318
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:08,820
Nami, no!

319
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:12,080
I can't move!

320
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:13,241
I'm freezing up!

321
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,060
Not again!

322
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:20,754
Don't let her get you!

323
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:26,420
All right, Katorea Manos!

324
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:27,950
Face!

325
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:34,970
Mommy!

326
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,760
She's so scary!

327
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:44,900
Sorry, but Master Caesar needs those
test subjects for an important project.

328
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:49,900
That's why it's my job, to ensure
he and the experiment are kept safe.

329
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:54,940
But now you've given Mocha
these rebellious ideas. Us!

330
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:58,517
They chose to leave this awful
place of their own free will!

331
00:17:58,600 --> 00:17:59,430
That's enough!

332
00:17:59,513 --> 00:18:00,343
Out of my way!

333
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:05,200
Go on, hurry up!

334
00:18:06,780 --> 00:18:08,300
Follow me! Right!

335
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:09,997
Hang in there, Mocha!

336
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,200
We're on our way!

337
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:14,560
That's not very nice.

338
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:18,377
Since the first day they came
to live on the island with us,

339
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:23,284
We've treated those children with every
comfort and kindness they could ever want.

340
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:26,917
And yet you're trying
to steal these beloved

341
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,620
treasures from their
adoring foster parents.

342
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:33,440
But I suppose you are pirates.

343
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:36,940
If you expect it, then
you must be fine with it.

344
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:39,140
I told you it's not nice.

345
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:41,320
You're done interfering.

346
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:43,660
Sword snow!

347
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:47,040
Skin sword technique!

348
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:59,537
You know, I've noticed that all you've
been doing is defending yourself.

349
00:18:59,620 --> 00:19:03,317
So is there some reason why you
haven't tried to attack me at all?

350
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:07,177
That's funny at first; I thought
there was no way I could defeat you.

351
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:08,517
How about that?

352
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:11,357
I guess I was mistaken—there's
another room back here.

353
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:13,957
Find the children and get
them out as fast as you can.

354
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:17,200
can It feels like a snowstorm in here.

355
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,360
The Navy.

356
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:21,080
Come on, let's bust the door open.

357
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:25,357
It doesn't matter how many of you
come to take those children away.

358
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:26,520
I'll stop you.

359
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:28,240
Save those kids!

360
00:19:29,220 --> 00:19:31,749
Why are all those
marines answering to you?

361
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:33,140
They're not here.

362
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:36,124
The only person I can see
is pirate hunter Zoro.

363
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:39,134
Of course that pain in the ass is here.

364
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:41,857
All right, here's the plan.

365
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:44,780
Everybody make dumb faces at Mosshead!

366
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:52,061
I hope they all slip on the ice
and crack their stupid skulls open.

367
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:56,966
Jackass, Nami and Robin
already went that way.

368
00:19:57,060 --> 00:19:59,660
Why don't you go chase them down? Gotcha!

369
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:02,392
I knew you would be useful to me one day!

370
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:03,920
You heard him, boys!

371
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:05,236
Let's go find the...

372
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:08,668
Never mind, we've got
a honey right in here!

373
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:12,260
Take those tail betters! Oh, come on!

374
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:14,674
Put your jaws up off the floor, morons!

375
00:20:15,820 --> 00:20:17,644
Wait, just look at her, though.

376
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:20,220
She's half woman, half bird.

377
00:20:20,740 --> 00:20:21,740
No way.

378
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:24,080
A real-life harpy. Huh?

379
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:27,560
Yeah, but hey.

380
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:30,671
Human or not, she sure is a looker, right?

381
00:20:31,020 --> 00:20:32,667
Sexiest bird I've ever seen.

382
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,337
Yeah, I could be into that.

383
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:35,250
Woo-hoo!

384
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:38,833
Call me crazy, but I think
you're actually enjoying this.

385
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:42,460
Hey, why is it snowing?

386
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:43,460
Are we inside?

387
00:20:43,820 --> 00:20:45,260
It's my duty, after all.

388
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:47,000
I don't care who you are.

389
00:20:47,140 --> 00:20:50,846
It'll be a cold day in hell when
I let you take those children.

390
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:08,200
It's my shoulder!

391
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:09,760
She bit it off!

392
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:11,240
You'll pay for that!

393
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:22,980
She's a Nokia-type!

394
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:25,820
Damn it, woman.

395
00:21:33,260 --> 00:21:35,480
Someone is using Haki on me.

396
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:40,560
Captain Seagy!

397
00:21:42,020 --> 00:21:46,020
We sealed off the doors to keep the
gas from getting into this room.

398
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:50,992
But we don't know that it won't
leak in from another spot.

399
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:56,746
We don't have much time, so do whatever
it takes and rescue all of the children!

400
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:57,910
What?

401
00:21:57,993 --> 00:21:58,980
But what about you?

402
00:22:00,380 --> 00:22:02,140
I'm going to stay right here.

403
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:06,544
If you ask me, you could
use a little help here.

404
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:07,910
What?
